        584,
        993,
        646
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The Civilian Life of the Women in the United States, 1918-1919, is a comprehensive study of the lives of American women from 1918 to 1919. It covers all aspects of daily life, from work and school to home and family, and includes descriptions of popular culture, social events, and political events. This book is not only a study of American life during this period, but also a look at the lives of the women themselves.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 18,
          "mean": -0.4592,
          "min": -2.1614
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
